{
  "summary": "Removes the `MAX_BIP125_RBF_SEQUENCE` constant from the functional test framework and eliminates its usage across wallet and non-wallet functional tests. Tests that previously used the constant to ensure non-final sequence numbers now use `MAX_SEQUENCE_NONFINAL` or default sequences. The constant is scoped strictly to `wallet_deprecated_rbf.py` to maintain coverage for deprecated BIP 125 RPC behavior until eventual removal.",
  "problem": "Functional tests throughout the test suite unnecessarily rely on BIP 125 opt-in sequence numbers even when BIP 125 signaling is irrelevant to the scenario under test, conflicting with ongoing efforts to deprecate and remove BIP 125 signaling logic from the codebase.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author description: 'Partially fixes https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/32661. This is in line with the removal and deprecation of BIP 125 RBF signalling from the codebase.'",
    "Commit 8e8765e46d: 'Remove the usage in all the tests where used except the ones where the sequence is set to unique values to avoid creating duplicate transactions simultaneously.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#35433"
    ],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "The PR branch currently includes 11 commits imported directly from prerequisite PR #35433 (deprecating the `replaceable` RPC argument and altering wallet defaults). Only the final two commits represent the scope of this PR.",
